    date "2022-06-29T23:25:03Z"
    title "Climate change forces major lifestyle changes high in the Himalayan mountains"
    description "Research published last year shows the massive Himalayan glaciers have shrunk 10-times faster over the past four decades than during the previous seven centuries. It threatens agriculture and the water supply for millions across South Asia. Fred de Sam Lazaro reports on one project aimed at blunting the environmental impact for communities in the Himalayas. &#10;&#10;Stream your PBS favorites with the PBS app: https://to.pbs.org/2Jb8twG&#160; Find more from PBS NewsHour at https://www.pbs.org/newshour&#160; Subscribe to our YouTube channel: https://bit.ly/2HfsCD6&#160; Follow us: TikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@pbsnews&#160;&#160;&#10;Twitter: http://www.twitter.com/newshour&#10;Instagram: http://www.instagram.com/newshour&#160;&#160;&#10;Facebook: http://www.pbs.org/newshour&#160; Subscribe: PBS NewsHour podcasts: https://www.pbs.org/newshour/podcasts&#10;Newsletters: https://www.pbs.org/newshour/subscribe"
