  [
    id 310
    label "3H1iH9wIFWU"
    step 0
    date "2022-04-05T07:18:19Z"
    title "Climate Change Solutions: New IPCC Report on How to Solve the Climate Change Problem"
    description "CLIMATE CHANGE REPORT&#10;The United Nations have released a massive report on climate change. The news isn't good, but they say we've still got time to fix some of the biggest effects of climate change if we get cracking. This new report from hundreds of climate scientists around the world says climate change is really close to getting out of control which could mean more extreme weather events like flooding, fires and land erosion. That doesn't sound good surely we can do something about it? Luckily, yes we can, but the report says some big changes need to happen, and that the current plans that governments around the world have to cut carbon emissions aren't going to be enough. Scientists say we need to stop burning things like coal and start using a lot more renewable energy like wind and solar power. Also, that we need to grow more forests and start eating less meat. The report even says we may need to use technology that sucks carbon emissions straight out of our atmosphere. It may sound like a lot, but according to the IPCC its all possible and pretty cheap, as long as governments and big businesses start to get on board.&#10;&#10;TAS PREMIER RESIGNS&#10;Tasmania's Premier has decided to quit politics. Peter Gutwein has led the Tasmanian Liberal government since 2020, and will step down as soon as the party elects a new leader. Gutwein says the past two years dealing with COVID have been tough and he's looking forward to spending more time with his family.&#10;&#10;SPACE MESSAGE&#10;A group of scientists from NASA have put together a message that they want to beam out into space to make contact with alien life! And as Jack found out, it's not the first time humans have tried this! While we're yet to make ACTUAL contact with aliens, we humans have certainly been trying to. The first interstellar message was beamed out in 1962 in morse code, then in 1974 a group of scientists in the US used two different radio frequencies to transmit a code which when arranged correctly. Includes things like numbers, elements for human life, the building blocks of DNA, an image of a human and our solar system. Other attempts of contact have included a chip commercial, a Beatles Song, and a gold record containing, amongst other things, whale noises. But so far, we've had no response. Now a group of Scientists from NASA have put together a new message: &#34;BEACON IN THE GALAXY&#34;. It's basically just an updated version of previous messages, and includes a return address. Something many people, including the late Stephen Hawking, have warned against. You know, in case the aliens we contact aren't friendly, or are just plain rude!&#10;&#10;DOG SWIM&#10;It's a dog's day out at the Glenorchy pool. They're going for a swim to celebrate the end of summer. And it looks like they're having a lot of fun. The pool is closing for the winter so it doesn't need to be kept clean enough for humans anymore. Which means our furry friends can have a dip in the pool too. And it's all for a good cause. Organisers have raised about $1000 for Guide Dogs Tasmania. About 100 dogs of all shapes and sizes made it to the event, chasing balls, wagging tails and of course doing the doggy paddle.&#10;__________________________________________&#10;Make sure to like &#38; subscribe to our videos if you want to stay in the know!&#10;&#128073; Subscribe https://www.youtube.com/behindthenews?sub_confirmation=1&#10;&#10;We have 1000s of stories on all sorts of topics - if you're looking for help to understand something, you'll probably find it on BTN http://www.abc.net.au/btn/ &#10;&#10;Follow us on Social Media:&#10;TikTok https://www.tiktok.com/@behindthenewstv&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/abcbtn &#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/behindthenews/ &#10;&#10;For the past 50 years, Behind the News has been helping to break down current issues and events for young people all around the world. The program is a high-energy, fun way for people to learn about the stories we see in the news while providing background information that isn&#8217;t usually given by other news bulletins."
    channeltitle "Behind the News"
