    date "2022-03-10T14:01:15Z"
    title "Effects of Climate Change in New York City | CUNY TV Special"
    description "Around New York City, the ocean currents are shifting. We're facing rising global sea levels. And consequently, there is more coastal flooding, storm surges,&#10; erosion, and property damage. As our temperatures rise, rainfall increases. So we're being hit with more floods and droughts. The CUNY TV Special - Effects of Climate Change in New York City examines all these issues and looks at the most significant threats&#10; facing our local communities.&#10;&#10;Guests:&#10;Vincent Lee - Civil Engineer, ARUP&#10;Deborah Balk - Professor, Marxe School/Baruch College&#10;Michael Dadap - The Children&#8217;s Orchestra Society&#10;Costa Costantinides - CEO, Variety Boys and Girls Club of Queens&#10;Dana Gumb - Bluebelt Project Lead, NYC Department of Environmental Protection&#10;Shannon Curley, Ph.D. - Adjunct Professor, CUNY College of Staten Island&#10;Jose Ramirez-Garofalo - Adjunct Lecturer, CUNY College of Staten Island&#10;Melissa Barber M.D. - Co-Founder, South Bronx Unite&#10;Liv Yoon, Ph.D. - Post Doctoral Research Scholar, Mailman School of Public Health - Earth Institute - Columbia University&#10;Mark Brescia - Con Edison&#10;John Nappo - Kingsborough Community College&#10;&#10;Recording Date &#10;02/10/2022&#10;First Air Date &#10;03/04/2022&#10;&#10;CUNY TV airs a variety of special programming throughout the year, from arts and music specials including opera and ballet, to public affairs program.&#10;&#10;Watch more CUNY TV Specials at https://tv.cuny.edu/homepage/show/cuny-tv-specials/&#10;&#10;Subscribe to the Series Playlist: https://bit.ly/3pQ3oBe&#10;Subscribe to the CUNY TV channel: https://bit.ly/2GmGb13&#10;&#10;Follow CUNY TV:&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/CUNYTV&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/cunytv&#10;Instagram:https://www.instagram.com/cuny_tv/&#10;YouTube:https://www.youtube.com/user/cunytv75 &#10;LinkedIn:https://www.linkedin.com/company/cunytv/&#10;Find more from CUNY TV at https://tv.cuny.edu&#10;&#10;CLSP01002 V1"
