    id 436
    label "QjAQ--6ceM8"
    step 0
    date "2022-04-23T19:00:08Z"
    title "The desert will surely disappear in 2024! Climate change in Saudi Arabia"
    description "Welcome to the planet news channel. Today we will tell you how climate change has affected the holy cities of all Muslims, located in a desert valley in the west of Saudi Arabia - Mecca and Taif.&#10;Taif has seen heavy rain in some parts of the province, while this rain has come to wash away the blow left by the dust wave that hit it recently and lasted for several days.&#10;Heavy rain, stronger and more comprehensive, on Saturday, warned of downwind and dusty waves.&#10;In the video, we see the torrents engulfing the Wadi and Taal Qiya, as well as papyrus on the Al Sedira road southeast of Taif.&#10;There has never been an invasion of locusts in Saudi Arabia caused by hot and dry weather that has settled in the Riyadh region.&#10;The National Meteorological Center expected that the possibilities for thunderstorms were ripe, accompanied by active winds at parts of the heights: (Jazan, Asir, Al-Baha) extending to parts of the heights of the regions of Mecca and Medina, and the sky would be partly cloudy, interspersed with thunderstorms and rain clouds.&#10;It is not excluded the formation of near-wall sandstorms caused by descending winds, which love thunderclouds in the areas of Medina, Hail and Qasim.&#10;In particular, more rains are expected in the coming days, and these rains can spread - God willing - to all parts of Taif and nearby governorates.&#10;Saudis exploded with videos of the rain as young Saudis seized the opportunity to show the country in a different light.&#10;Authorities have warned people of heavy rain and thunderstorms in Mecca, Medina, Al Baha, Jazan with possible severe flooding in the Eastern Province, Riyadh and Qassim, as well as light rain in Jawf, Tabuk and on the northern borders.&#10;&#10;The channel lists natural disasters such as:&#10;1) emergency geological situations: earthquake, volcanic eruption, mudflow, landslide, collapse, avalanche;&#10;2) Hydrological emergencies: flood, tsunami, limnological catastrophe, floods, flooding;&#10;3) Fires: forest fire, peat fire, glass fire, forest fire;&#10;4) Extreme meteorological situations: Tornado, Cyclone, Snowstorm, Hail, Drought, Hail, Hurricane, Storm, Thunderstorm, Typhoon, Storm, Lightning.&#10;&#10;The desert is sinking! Heavy rains in Saudi Arabia flood Taif&#10;https://youtu.be/gW4VmRrJLpc&#10;&#10;Arabs are choking! Dust storm hits Saudi Arabia&#10;https://youtu.be/r7r9qcEHWGQ&#10;&#10;flood 2022 playlist&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bTG5If4IiAk&#38;list=PLHWMqs-B5OVCEEBV8UR-REgUvFNmaIpzv&#10;&#10;#weather #news #earthquake #makkah #granizo #rain #taif #saudiarabia #flood #flooding #flooddesert #desert #floodtaif #arabia"
