    date "2021-06-11T10:24:05Z"
    title "Local and Indigenous Knowledge in Climate Change Adaptation"
    description "As part of SLYCAN Trust&#8217;s research on climate and disaster risk and risk transfer in Sri Lanka, our team engages with primary food producers and farming communities to understand how climate change impacts their livelihoods and how they manage climate risks. These insights are documented in a series of video interviews with farmers in the Sri Lankan dry zone districts of Anuradhapura and Trincomalee, in an attempt to share their realities with a wider audience and amplify their voices.&#10;&#10;Local and Indigenous Knowledge in Climate Change Adaptation&#10;Interview with Ms. Chandra Galagoda from Trincomalee district, Sri Lanka&#10;&#10;The video has been developed by SLYCAN Trust as part of the project &#34;Multi-Actor Partnership on Climate and Disaster Risk Finance and Preparedness in the Context of the InsuResilience Global Partnership,&#34; which is supported by the German Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ).&#10;&#10;SLYCAN Trust is also on: &#10;Website: http://slycantrust.org/&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/slycantrust/&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/SLYCANTrust&#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/slycantrust/&#10;&#10;Email: info@slycantrust.org"
