    date "2022-06-20T21:43:29Z"
    title "CATACLYSMS: JUNE 20, 2022! earthquakes, climate change, volcano, tsunami, natural disasters,news"
    description "CATACLYSMS: JUNE 20, 2022! earthquakes, climate change, volcano, tsunami, natural disasters,news&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Forest fires due to unprecedented heat waves rage in Germany&#10;The fire spread to almost 200 hectares. Firefighters are still battling the elements. The Potsdam-Mittelmark district authorities had to call for additional help. Sunday's high winds also made the situation worse. Rescue workers had to evacuate residents in three districts.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Dust storms and strong winds caused panic in Calvados resorts, France&#10;Strong winds literally swept over the coast of the French department of Calvados for half an hour &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Miami's luxury car garage flooded: sad video&#10;Video from the USA which captures the horrific consequences of the flooding, is spreading online.&#10;The storm, which flooded Florida in June, caused the flooding of one of underground garages in Miami. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Millions of people affected by flooding in India&#10;At least 4228,000 citizens have been affected by the floods, according to the Indian Disaster Management Authority. The regional administration of the states reports that 71 people died. The states of Assam and Meghalaya were the hardest hit by the bad weather.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Huge hail hit car windows and roofs in France from the night to the morning of June 20.&#10;On the night of Sunday to Monday, several departments were hit by large hail that fell in Endre and Loire-et-Cher in Aquitaine hailstones the size of golf balls.  &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Heavy rains in southern China caused floods that demolished homes and cars. On Saturday and Sunday, the amount of rain in some places was the heaviest in 60 years, experts said. &#10;Social media users show videos of streets turned into full-flowing rivers, carrying away cars and single-story structures. In one of the houses swept away by the water, five people died.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;A devastating tornado struck China,&#10;A terrifying vortex swept through coastal areas, sweeping away everything in its path. The vortex came on suddenly, eyewitnesses say. The speed exceeded 10 meters per second. Several residential houses in the southern provinces were destroyed and power lines collapsed. Residents in fear were filming what was happening outside their windows. Those who were caught in the street tried to dodge heavy objects flying everywhere. Now city services are removing the rubble and trying to free the roads from the fallen trees. There have been no reports of casualties or injuries so far.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Hundreds of thousands of homes are under water because of severe flooding in Bangladesh&#10;Authorities reported that two areas in the northeast of the country are flooded. They are located on the banks of the Surma River. According to the Minister of Disaster Management, the flooding may be the worst in 122 years. Local residents are being helped to evacuate from the disaster zone. About 90,000 residents of Sylhet and Sunamganj districts are currently staying in temporary accommodation facilities. UN climate change experts predict that about 17% of the country's population will need to be resettled over the next decade if global warming continues at the current rate. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;The channel lists such natural disasters as:&#10;1) Geological emergencies: Earthquake, volcanic eruption, mudflow, landslide, landfall, avalanche;&#10;2) Hydrological emergencies:  Flood, Tsunami, Limnological catastrophe, floods, flooding;&#10;3) Fires: Forest fire, Peat fire, Glass Fire, Wildfire;&#10;4) Meteorological emergencies: Tornado, Cyclone, Blizzard, Hail, Drought, Hail, Hurricane, Storm, Thunderstorm, typhoon, Tempest, Lightning.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;If you find any improper use of your copyrighted content (videos, photos and music) in the video, please contact us by  e-mail specified in the &#34;about the channel&#34; tab.&#10;&#10;ATTENTION: Video material is taken from social networks. It is selected by date of publication, title, description and location of the event. Sometimes, due to unscrupulous posting of news on social networks, the video may contain fragments that do not correspond to the date and place. It is not always possible to check their reliability. Thank you for your understanding.&#10;&#10;In 2022, natural disasters have become more frequent. We are seeing climate change in many countries around the world. It is not yet known how 2022 will begin.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;#breakingnews #tsunami #earthquake #tsunamiTonga #meteor #meteorBrazil #meteorMinasGerais #greeceSnow #stormDiomedes #windMinsk #windBelarus #HungaTonga  #flood #earthquake #tornado  #flashflood #flooding #flooding2022 #severestorm #landslide #windstorm #waterspout #storm #hailstorm #volcanoeruption #flood #flooding #flashfloods #landslide #fire #snowstorm #flooding2022 #mothernatureangry #caughtoncamera #cataclysm #weather #naturaldisasters #naturaldisasters2022 #news #newsjanuary15 #agonyofmotherearth&#10; #weather #news #earthquake #tsunami #ndn #rain #toulouse #france #garonne #ari&#232;ge #flood #lluvia #europe"
