    step 0
    date "2022-04-04T16:28:45Z"
    title "Will politicians listen to climate change warnings? | Inside Story"
    description "For more than a century industrialisation has spread across much of the world.&#13;&#10;The planet is getting warmer and the places on it, where humanity can live healthily, are getting fewer.&#13;&#10;The UN's Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change - or IPCC - has brought together scientists from 195 countries to solve the problem.&#13;&#10;In the last eight months, it's published two reports looking at the causes and effects of climate change.&#13;&#10;Its third one has just been released, suggesting what we can do to reverse the damage.&#13;&#10;So what should be done to limit this damage? &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Presenter: Rob Matheson&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Guests:&#13;&#10; &#13;&#10;Andy Reisinger - Member of the Bureau of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change and Vice-Chair of Working Group III (Mitigation).&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Syeda Rizwana Hasan - Chief Executive of the Bangladesh Environmental Lawyers Association and Goldman Environmental Prize winner.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Stephan Singer - Senior Climate Science and Global Energy Policy Adviser at Climate Action Network International.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;- Follow us on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AJEnglish/&#13;&#10;- Find us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/aljazeera/&#13;&#10;- Check our website: https://www.aljazeera.com/&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;#ClimateChange #GlobalWarming"
