  [
    id 492
    label "20iWKGYN_Uc"
    step 0
    date "2022-06-18T20:36:23Z"
    title "CATACLYSMS: JUNE 18, 2022! earthquakes, climate change, volcano, tsunami, natural disasters,news"
    description "CATACLYSMS: JUNE 18, 2022! earthquakes, climate change, volcano, tsunami, natural disasters,news&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Severe hail has hit Tuscany, Italy.&#10;The most frightening event today in Italy, was a devastating hailstorm with hailstones up to 5 cm in diameter, north of Florence. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;At least one person died in a fire at a petrochemical complex in Shanghai on Saturday, &#10;The fire broke out at the ethylene glycol plant of Sinopec Petrochemical Complex at about 4 a.m. in the city's Jinshan district&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Unceasing rains continue to sow panic in India &#10;In Dangar, five family members were killed in a landslide.&#10;The flooding situation in the state of Assam and the state of Bangladesh . At least 25 people died because of flooding caused by rain. 4 million people stranded in Sylhet, Sunamganj because of flooding. Sylhet International Airport closed, Bangladesh state.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;The area of fires in Russia has already reached almost 50 thousand hectares&#10; as of June 18, in Russia there are 52 forest fires on the area of 24,987 hectares which are under active suppression. Most of them are in Chukotka (20,400 hectares).&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Today, there are nine sunspot groups on the solar disk, which is the maximum in many years.&#10;If only one of them has an outburst, a geomagnetic storm could occur on Earth. The AR3031 sunspot with an unstable beta-gamma magnetic field, which stores energy for M-class solar flares, is the most likely to &#34;explode.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Tropical Storm Celia is moving toward El Salvador, Guatemala and southern Mexico. This is reported on its website by the National Hurricane Watch Center USA .&#10;It moves from the Pacific Ocean at a speed of 65 km / h and is expected to reach the coasts of these countries June 19, causing heavy rains. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;The abnormally warm winter may have caused the mass death of seals in the Caspian Sea, the Committee of Fisheries of the Ministry of Ecology suggested&#10;Half of the carcasses found were young animals that live only on ice floes until a certain time. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;After heavy rains and thunderstorms in the Atlantic Ocean hit the East Coast yesterday, some parts of Miami received heavy rains that flooded several streets downtown and around Biscayne Boulevard. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;A large dust cloud covers Dakar&#10;The images show that visibility in one of the most densely populated West African cities is close to zero. Specialists have warned residents about deteriorating air quality. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;In China, the province of Inner Mongolia was under the power of a terrible sandstorm. This natural cataclysm reduced visibility to zero in just a few seconds and made the air unfit for breathing. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;In the Philippines, in the province of Sorsogon, volcano Bulusan threw a column of red-hot steam and ash. There is no information about casualties, casualties and other consequences of the eruption. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Terrible warehouse fire in Bangladesh&#10;The death toll from a massive fire that broke out last night at a shipping container depot in the Bangladeshi port of Chittagong has risen to 25 people.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Heavy rains have caused landslides and flooding in some regions of Sri Lanka. The National Disaster Management Center has set a high level of meteorological danger on the island.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;The channel lists such natural disasters as:&#10;1) Geological emergencies: Earthquake, volcanic eruption, mudflow, landslide, landfall, avalanche;&#10;2) Hydrological emergencies:  Flood, Tsunami, Limnological catastrophe, floods, flooding;&#10;3) Fires: Forest fire, Peat fire, Glass Fire, Wildfire;&#10;4) Meteorological emergencies: Tornado, Cyclone, Blizzard, Hail, Drought, Hail, Hurricane, Storm, Thunderstorm, typhoon, Tempest, Lightning.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;If you find any improper use of your copyrighted content (videos, photos and music) in the video, please contact us by  e-mail specified in the &#34;about the channel&#34; tab.&#10;&#10;ATTENTION: Video material is taken from social networks. It is selected by date of publication, title, description and location of the event. Sometimes, due to unscrupulous posting of news on social networks, the video may contain fragments that do not correspond to the date and place. It is not always possible to check their reliability. Thank you for your understanding.&#10;&#10;In 2022, natural disasters have become more frequent. We are seeing climate change in many countries around the world. It is not yet known how 2022 will begin.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;#breakingnews #tsunami #earthquake #tsunamiTonga #meteor #meteorBrazil #meteorMinasGerais #greeceSnow #stormDiomedes #windMinsk #windBelarus #HungaTonga  #flood #earthquake #tornado  #flashflood #flooding #flooding2022 #severestorm #landslide #windstorm #waterspout #storm #hailstorm #volcanoeruption #flood #flooding #flashfloods #landslide #fire #snowstorm #flooding2022 #mothernatureangry #caughtoncamera #cataclysm #weather #naturaldisasters #naturaldisasters2022 #news #newsjanuary15 #agonyofmotherearth&#10; #weather #news #earthquake #tsunami #ndn #rain #toulouse #france #garonne #ari&#232;ge #flood #lluvia #europe"
