    title "CATACLYSMS: JUNE 17, 2022! earthquakes, climate change, volcano, tsunami, natural disasters,news"
    description "CATACLYSMS: JUNE 17, 2022! earthquakes, climate change, volcano, tsunami, natural disasters,news&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Severe storm and tornado in parts of Southern Ontario, Canada.&#10;The storm downed trees and power lines, leaving thousands of people without power.&#10;The storm now ranks sixth in Canadian history in terms of insured losses, surpassing the 2005 Toronto flood, local officials said.&#10;The devastation caused widespread property damage, significant power outages.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;A tornado in the USA overturns trucks, blocks highways and rips out trees by the hundreds, scattering debris and destroying houses like houses of cards. This natural apocalypse occurred in Wisconsin.A tornado in the state left 2,000 homes without electricity.&#10;Due to fallen trees and broken power lines more than 100 thousand residents of Wisconsin were left without electricity. &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Heavy rains caused flooding around Cape Town and the Western Cape province of South Africa&#10;Rescuers responded to calls more than 100 times in Cape Town, mostly due to blocked storm drains, flooding and the threat of flooding in some areas.&#10;City officials said up to 128 mm of rain fell at Newlands Station during the 24-hour period &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;China faces record rainfall, intense heat and tornadoes&#10;The southern Chinese metropolis of Guangzhou experienced a rare combination of record rainfall, intense heat and tornadoes this week. Millions of residents were displaced, property damaged, farmland flooded&#10;Meteorologists predict that rainfall in southern China will continue until June 21.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;In Jorpeland, Norway, a hiker managed to capture an avalanche on video. The video went viral on social media&#10;The girl was strolling through a popular tourist area when she heard a rumbling sound from above and pointed her camera up just in time: an avalanche came down the mountainside.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Nearly a thousand hectares of forest and bushes have burned as a result of wildfires in the Spanish region of Catalonia&#10;Three wildfires caused by record high temperatures are raging near the towns of Baldomar, Corbera d'Ebre and Castellar-Ribera. Hundreds of firefighters are extinguishing the fires from the ground and aviation is also involved.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;About 300,000 people in the Sylhet district of northeastern Bangladesh were affected by floods&#10;Heavy rains flooded low-lying areas, including homes, roads, schools and stores. Over 300 villages were submerged. Road connections were interrupted. Authorities have set up 42 shelters for flood victims.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;Up to 40,000 hectares of crops and potential crops were partially or completely destroyed as a result of heavy hail that struck the southern and southeastern parts of Bulgaria. &#10;According to preliminary data, the greatest damage to agriculture occurred in the districts of Madan, Rodopi and Tvarditsa, as well as in the Burgas and Kardzhali regions.&#10;Chunks of ice broke through the roofs of buildings and damaged vehicles in some settlements. There were no dead or injured among the people.&#10;As noted in the statement of the Department of Emergency Situations, the losses incurred by these areas run into hundreds of thousands of dollars.&#10;The Bulgarian government is considering the possibility of providing financial compensation to the victims.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;The channel lists such natural disasters as:&#10;1) Geological emergencies: Earthquake, volcanic eruption, mudflow, landslide, landfall, avalanche;&#10;2) Hydrological emergencies:  Flood, Tsunami, Limnological catastrophe, floods, flooding;&#10;3) Fires: Forest fire, Peat fire, Glass Fire, Wildfire;&#10;4) Meteorological emergencies: Tornado, Cyclone, Blizzard, Hail, Drought, Hail, Hurricane, Storm, Thunderstorm, typhoon, Tempest, Lightning.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;If you find any improper use of your copyrighted content (videos, photos and music) in the video, please contact us by  e-mail specified in the &#34;about the channel&#34; tab.&#10;&#10;ATTENTION: Video material is taken from social networks. It is selected by date of publication, title, description and location of the event. Sometimes, due to unscrupulous posting of news on social networks, the video may contain fragments that do not correspond to the date and place. It is not always possible to check their reliability. Thank you for your understanding.&#10;&#10;In 2022, natural disasters have become more frequent. We are seeing climate change in many countries around the world. It is not yet known how 2022 will begin.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;#breakingnews #tsunami #earthquake #tsunamiTonga #meteor #meteorBrazil #meteorMinasGerais #greeceSnow #stormDiomedes #windMinsk #windBelarus #HungaTonga  #flood #earthquake #tornado  #flashflood #flooding #flooding2022 #severestorm #landslide #windstorm #waterspout #storm #hailstorm #volcanoeruption #flood #flooding #flashfloods #landslide #fire #snowstorm #flooding2022 #mothernatureangry #caughtoncamera #cataclysm #weather #naturaldisasters #naturaldisasters2022 #news #newsjanuary15 #agonyofmotherearth&#10; #weather #news #earthquake #tsunami #ndn #rain #toulouse #france #garonne #ari&#232;ge #flood #lluvia #europe"
